<title>GERMANY: Siemens in group winning Danish rail order.</title>
<headline>Siemens in group winning Danish rail order.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Siemens AG said on Monday it was a member of a consortium which had won a 1.6 billion mark ($949.2 million) contract from the Danish state railways to supply 112 commuter railway vehicles.</p>
<p>Siemens said in a statement the consortium was led by Linke-Hofmann-Busch GmbH and included GEC Alsthom Transport.</p>
<p>First deliveries will be in February 1999 and the order will be completed by 2005.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.685 German Marks)</p>
</text>
